## 9. Architecture and Implementation

### 9.1 System Architecture

The grounded agent has three modules with strict information-flow constraints. The **Belief Module** maintains an exact Bayesian posterior over $\mathcal{H}$ by enumeration; no self-generated data ever enters it. The **Policy Module** is a stochastic policy $\pi_\theta$ mapping the posterior probability vector and normalised step index to a distribution over queries; for the symbolic regression testbed the output is a Gaussian over $\mathcal{X} \subset \mathbb{R}$. The **Meta-Learner** is an outer loop updating $\theta$ using only held-out oracle test pairs for evaluation — never the agent's own predictions.

The architecture of the policy network: input is the $H$-dimensional posterior vector concatenated with $k/K$; two hidden layers of 128 units with ReLU activations; output is the mean and log-variance of a Gaussian over $\mathcal{X} = [-5, 5]$ with variance clamped to enforce minimum exploration $\sigma \ge 0.1$.

### 9.2 Symbolic Regression Testbed

Grammar: arithmetic expressions over $\{+, -, \times, \div, \sin, \cos, \exp, \log\}$, constants $\{0, 1, 2, \pi, e\}$, variable $x$, depth at most 4. Exhaustive generation with semantic duplicate removal yields $|\mathcal{H}| \approx 10^4$–$10^5$. Input domain: $\mathcal{X} = [-5, 5]$, discretised to 1000 points for evaluation. Oracle: noiseless function evaluation.

### 9.3 Meta-Training Algorithm

```
Initialise θ
for meta-iteration = 1, 2, … do
    Sample M tasks {h_i} ~ T_train
    for each task h_i do
        P ← uniform prior
        for k = 1 to K do
            x_k ~ π_θ( · | P, k/K)
            y_k ← h_i(x_k)                   // oracle only
            P ← BayesUpdate(P, (x_k, y_k))    // no self-data
        end
        Δ_i ← progress on held-out oracle test set
    end
    θ ← θ + η_t · (1/M) Σ_i Δ_i Σ_k ∇_θ log π_θ(x_k | s_k)
end
```

Training details: Adam optimiser, initial lr $10^{-3}$, decay $\eta_t = \eta_0/(1+\beta t)$; mini-batch $M = 32$; horizon $K = 10$; linear value baseline for variance reduction; evaluation every 100 iterations on 100 validation tasks.

